Palm's Location Services app.

com.palm.app.location as it is on the reference TouchPad (webOS CE 3.1.0), copied from
/usr/palm/applications on 2026-11-07. Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard; never released
under an open licence; distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo and the Prelude fonts.
codepoet approved bundling it with Lunacy's changes, 2026-11-07.

It sets how webOS apps and websites get the device's location from Lunacy's location service
(palm://com.palm.location, AndroidLuna's LocationService.kt), which answers from Android's
location: "GPS" is Android's GPS, "Google Services" its network location. Android's own
location switch and its permission for Lunacy are Android's; Lunacy's First Use asks for the
permission.

Lunacy's change, marked [Lunacy] in the source:

- app/controllers/main-assistant.js (two places): the "Background data collection" switch, which let Google
  collect location data through Palm's long-gone Google location service, stays hidden.

What needs no change, because the service answers as Lunacy is: Palm's Google terms of use
never show (the service reports them accepted; Android's network location has its own
consent), and Geotag Photos, the TouchPad Camera's, stays hidden (the service reports no
camera, as Palm's app expects on a device without one).
